# makemytrip-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy this file to `.env` next to the scripts and fill in what you use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is in .gitignore. Keep it there. A secret passed on a command line
# is readable by anything that can run `ps` and lands in your shell history,
# which is why none of these has a flag you are expected to type.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#
#     explicit CLI flag  >  exported environment variable  >  .env  >  default
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any secret:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# Every variable below is one this code actually reads, and every variable
# the code reads is below. smoke_test.py asserts the two sets are equal in
# both directions.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: from a datacentre address this site serves nothing at
# all, so you need ONE of the two exits below. Measured 2026-09-24 from a
# netcup VPS (AS197540):
#
#     plain curl, curl's own User-Agent        HTTP 403, Akamai "Access Denied"
#     curl with a Chrome User-Agent             connection reset / hang
#     headless and headful Chromium             net::ERR_HTTP2_PROTOCOL_ERROR
#     the listing API itself (mapi.)            HTTP 403, Akamai "Access Denied"
#     2Captcha residential exits (eu, na, in)   net::ERR_HTTP2_PROTOCOL_ERROR
#     the Scraping Browser, country-in          HTTP 200, the full listing
#
# There is no captcha on the way in: Akamai refuses by dropping the
# connection, and there is nothing on the page to solve.


# --- 2Captcha -------------------------------------------------------------
# One key, four separately-billed products: captcha solving, the Scraping
# Browser API, proxies and fingerprints. https://2captcha.com
#
# No captcha was met on this site: 0 site-owned captcha markers on every
# served page, and Akamai's refusals carry no widget. The key is wired for
# the family's detection and solve path in case one appears, and it is what
# --fingerprint uses (a separate subscription from solving).
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- Scraping Browser API -------------------------------------------------
# A remote browser you do not run or patch, with a persistent profile and a
# chosen exit country. Used by --cdp-endpoint. THIS is the path measured to
# work: `country-in`, 4 of 6 fresh connections served on the first try on
# 2026-09-24, and the other two were a connection reset and a timeout that a
# re-connect cleared (the service picked a different Indian exit).
#
#   country-  picks the exit country. Use `in`. Prices are in INR whatever
#             the exit, because the currency follows the site's region.
#   pid-      a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection each,
#             capped per account. Reuse pids rather than minting one per
#             run, and expect a 500 (`profile_locked`, exit 5) while another
#             run still holds this one.
#
# Selenium cannot use this: chromedriver's `debuggerAddress` takes a bare
# host:port with nowhere to put a password. Playwright and pyppeteer can.
#
# The credentials in a profile expire in about a day, so never paste a
# working one anywhere that is committed.
MAKEMYTRIP_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-in-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- Proxy ----------------------------------------------------------------
# One URL here, or --proxy-file with one per line for a pool.
#
# NOT measured to work: three 2Captcha residential logins (eu, na, and one
# with -region-in) all ended in net::ERR_HTTP2_PROTOCOL_ERROR from local
# Chromium on this machine, 2026-09-24. Whether that is the exits or this
# machine's own Chromium being scored has not been separated, so treat the
# proxy path as untested rather than as broken.
#
# The credentials never reach the browser's command line: they go through
# the driver's own fields, and logs mask them while keeping host and port.
# Selenium's --proxy-server cannot authenticate at all, so that engine
# strips the credentials and warns.
MAKEMYTRIP_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@xx.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- Default target -------------------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url. A hotel listing address as the site builds it:
#
#   https://www.makemytrip.com/hotels/hotel-listing/?checkin=11102026&checkout=11112026&city=CTGOI&locusId=CTGOI&locusType=city&country=IN&roomStayQualifier=2e0e
#
# Only the query in the address is read; the flags (--city, --checkin,
# --checkout, --adults ...) do the same without a URL.
MAKEMYTRIP_URL=https://www.makemytrip.com/hotels/hotel-listing/?checkin=11102026&checkout=11112026&city=CTGOI&locusId=CTGOI&locusType=city&country=IN&roomStayQualifier=2e0e

# Deliberately NOT here: an output prefix. `--out` already carries a
# non-empty default, so the loader, which only fills UNSET values, would
# never see it. The variable would be silently inert.
